# Suppressions for the blocking scan:web-image-trivy job (passed with
# --ignorefile web/.trivyignore in .gitlab-ci.yml). One entry per CVE, with the
# reason in the comment directly above it. Re-verify an entry when the base
# image (node:22-alpine) or next changes; delete it once the scan stops
# reporting the id (checked against the image built from main on 2026-11-10).
#
# CVE-2026-33671: picomatch ReDoS. Trivy reports picomatch 4.0.3 at
# usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/picomatch/package.json, i.e. the
# copy bundled inside the npm CLI of the node:22-alpine base image (not at
# the app's picomatch). The app's own dependency is picomatch >= 4.0.7 (see
# web/package.json), and the compiled copy under next/dist/compiled/picomatch
# carries no version field, so it is not flagged. The runtime command is
# `node server.js`; npm is never executed in the container, so the bundled copy
# is not reachable.
CVE-2026-33671
